# Rust
#
# Generally, you should bind to a specific version of Cargo (the Rust
# package manager) in your `rust-toolchain.toml` file. This helps ensure
# that your project produces consistent builds and passes tests even when
# new versions of Rust are released. You also need to make sure that the
# `rust-toolchain.toml` file is *not* ignored by Git.

# Dependency directories
target/

# Normal Cargo artifacts
Cargo.lock # Usually committed for applications, ignored for libraries

# Generated file by rpi_rx_rust
output.csv

# Rust IDEs (e.g. VS Code with rust-analyzer)
.rust-analyzer/
.vscode/

# Build artifacts
*.d
*.o

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
.history

# Test/profiling
/test/
/benches/
/examples/
